    <h2>It doesn't replace your front desk. It covers what they can't.</h2>
    <p>Your desk person knows your patients, your providers and your schedule — that's not something to automate away, and this doesn't try to. It takes the hours nobody is there, the calls that arrive while both lines are busy, and the messages that pile up over a weekend. Everything else still goes to the person your patients already know.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
